malizedAlgorithm = webidl.converters[desiredType](\n    { __proto__: algorithm\x2C name: algName }\x2C\n    kNormalizeAlgorithmOpts\x2C\n  );\n  // 7.\n  normalizedAlgorithm.name = algName;\n\n  // 9. 10. Pre-computed keys and types from simpleAlgorithmDictionaries.\n  const dictMeta = simpleAlgorithmDictionaries[desiredType];\n  if (dictMeta) {\n    const { keys: dictKeys\x2C types: dictTypes } = dictMeta;\n    for (let i = 0; i < dictKeys.length; i++) {\n      const member = dictKeys[i];\n      const idlType = dictTypes[member];\n      const idlValue = normalizedAlgorithm[member];\n      // 3.\n      if (idlType === 'BufferSource' && idlValue) {\n        normalizedAlgorithm[member] = TypedArrayPrototypeSlice(\n          getBufferSourceBytes(idlValue)\x2C\n        );\n      } else if (idlType === 'HashAlgorithmIdentifier') {\n        normalizedAlgorithm[member] = normalizeAlgorithm(idlValue\x2C 'digest');\n      } else if (idlType === 'AlgorithmIdentifier') {\n        // This extension point is not used by any supported algorithm (yet?)\n        throw lazyDOMException('Not implemented.'\x2C 'NotSupportedError');\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return normalizedAlgorithm;\n}\n\nfunction getDataViewOrTypedArrayBuffer(V) {\n  return isDataView(V) ?\n    DataViewPrototypeGetBuffer(V) : TypedArrayPrototypeGetBuffer(V);\n}\n\nfunction getDataViewOrTypedArrayByteOffset(V) {\n  return isDataView(V) ?\n    DataViewPrototypeGetByteOffset(V) : TypedArrayPrototypeGetByteOffset(V);\n}\n\nfunction getDataViewOrTypedArrayByteLength(V) {\n  return isDataView(V) ?\n    DataViewPrototypeGetByteLength(V) : TypedArrayPrototypeGetByteLength(V);\n}\n\nfunction getBufferSourceByteLength(V) {\n  return ArrayBufferIsView(V) ?\n    getDataViewOrTypedArrayByteLength(V) :\n    ArrayBufferPrototypeGetByteLength(V);\n}\n\nfunction getBufferSourceBytes(V) {\n  return ArrayBufferIsView(V) ?\n    new Uint8Array(\n      getDataViewOrTypedArrayBuffer(V)\x2C\n      getDataViewOrTypedArrayByteOffset(V)\x2C\n      getDataViewOrTypedArrayByteLength(V)\x2C\n    ) :\n    new Uint8Array(V\x2C 0\x2C ArrayBufferPrototypeGetByteLength(V));\n}\n\nfunction getOptionalByteLength(V) {\n  return V === undefined ? 0 : TypedArrayPrototypeGetByteLength(V);\n}\n\nfunction hasAnyNotIn(set\x2C checks) {\n  for (const s of set)\n    if (!ArrayPrototypeIncludes(checks\x2C s))\n      return true;\n  return false;\n}\n\nconst validateByteSource = hideStackFrames((val\x2C name) => {\n  val = toBuf(val);\n\n  if (isAnyArrayBuffer(val) || isArrayBufferView(val))\n    return val;\n\n  throw new ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE.HideStackFramesError(\n    name\x2C\n    [\n      'string'\x2C\n      'ArrayBuffer'\x2C\n      'TypedArray'\x2C\n      'DataView'\x2C\n      'Buffer'\x2C\n    ]\x2C\n    val);\n});\n\n/**\n * @template T\n * @typedef {{ run(): Promise<T> }} WebCryptoJob\n */\n\n/**\n * CryptoJob constructors can synchronously throw while running their native\n * AdditionalConfig hook. WebCrypto needs those operation-specific setup\n * failures to reject with an OperationError.\n * @template T\n * @param {() => WebCryptoJob<T>} getJob\n * @returns {Promise<T>}\n */\nfunction jobPromise(getJob) {\n  try {\n    return getJob().run();\n  } catch (err) {\n    return PromiseReject(lazyDOMException(\n      'The operation failed for an operation-specific reason'\x2C\n      { name: 'OperationError'\x2C cause: err }));\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Temporarily shadow inherited then accessors on WebCrypto result objects.\n * Promise resolution reads "then" synchronously for thenable assimilation.\n * Returning an own undefined data property keeps that lookup from reaching\n * user-mutated prototypes.\n * @param {unknown} value\n * @returns {boolean}\n */\nfunction prepareWebCryptoResult(value) {\n  if ((value === null || typeof value !== 'object') &&\n      typeof value !== 'function') {\n    return false;\n  }\n  if (isPromise(value) || ObjectPrototypeHasOwnProperty(value\x2C 'then'))\n    return false;\n  setOwnProperty(value\x2C 'then'\x2C undefined);\n  return true;\n}\n\n/**\n * Remove the temporary then property installed by prepareWebCryptoResult().\n * @param {{ then?: unknown }} value\n * @returns {void}\n */\nfunction cleanupWebCryptoResult(value) {\n  delete value.then;\n}\n\n/**\n * @template T\n * @typedef {(value: T | PromiseLike<T>) => void} WebCryptoResolve\n */\n\n/**\n * Resolve a WebCrypto promise while inherited then accessors are shadowed.\n * @template T\n * @param {WebCryptoResolve<T>} resolve\n * @param {T | PromiseLike<T>} value\n * @returns {void}\n */\nfunction resolveWebCryptoResult(resolve\x2C value) {\n  const shouldCleanupResult = prepareWebCryptoResult(value);\n  try {\n    resolve(value);\n  } finally {\n    if (shouldCleanupResult)\n      cleanupWebCryptoResult(value);\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Run a WebCrypto promise reaction and settle the outer promise.\n * @template T\n * @template TResult\n * @param {((value: T) => TResult | PromiseLike<TResult>) | undefined} handler\n * @param {WebCryptoResolve<T | TResult>} resolve\n * @param {(reason?: unknown) => void} reject\n * @param {T} value\n * @param {boolean} isRejected\n * @returns {void}\n */\nfunction settleJobPromise(handler\x2C resolve\x2C reject\x2C value\x2C isRejected) {\n  try {\n    if (typeof handler === 'function') {\n      resolveWebCryptoResult(resolve\x2C handler(value));\n    } else if (isRejected) {\n      reject(value);\n    } else {\n      resolveWebCryptoResult(resolve\x2C value);\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    reject(err);\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Promise.prototype.then gets promise.constructor to determine the result\n * promise's species. These promises are internal WebCrypto intermediates\x2C so\n * make that lookup stay on the promise itself instead of user-mutated state.\n * @template T\n * @template [TResult1=T]\n * @template [TResult2=never]\n * @param {Promise<T>} promise\n * @param {((value: T) => TResult1 | PromiseLike<TResult1>) | null | undefined} [onFulfilled]\n * @param {((reason: unknown) => TResult2 | PromiseLike<TResult2>) | null | undefined} [onRejected]\n * @returns {Promise<TResult1 | TResult2>}\n */\nfunction jobPromiseThen(promise\x2C onFulfilled\x2C onRejected) {\n  const {\n    promise: resultPromise\x2C\n    resolve\x2C\n    reject\x2C\n  } = PromiseWithResolvers();\n  setOwnProperty(promise\x2C 'constructor'\x2C undefined);\n  PromisePrototypeThen(\n    promise\x2C\n    (value) => settleJobPromise(onFulfilled\x2C resolve\x2C reject\x2C value\x2C false)\x2C\n    (value) => settleJobPromise(onRejected\x2C resolve\x2C reject\x2C value\x2C true));\n  return resultPromise;\n}\n\n// In WebCrypto\x2C the publicExponent option in RSA is represented as a\n// WebIDL "BigInteger"... that is\x2C a Uint8Array that allows an arbitrary\n// number of leading zero bits. Our conventional APIs for reading\n// an unsigned int from a Buffer are not adequate. The implementation\n// here is adapted from the chromium implementation here:\n// https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/HEAD/third_party/blink/public/platform/web_crypto_algorithm_params.h\x2C but ported to JavaScript\n// Returns undefined if the conversion was unsuccessful.\nfunction bigIntArrayToUnsignedInt(input) {\n  let result = 0;\n  const length = TypedArrayPrototypeGetLength(input);\n\n  for (let n = 0; n < length; ++n) {\n    const n_reversed = length - n - 1;\n    if (n_reversed >= 4 && input[n])\n      return;  // Too large\n    result |= input[n] << 8 * n_reversed;\n  }\n\n  return result >>> 0;\n}\n\nfunction bigIntArrayToUnsignedBigInt(input) {\n  let result = 0n;\n  const length = TypedArrayPrototypeGetLength(input);\n\n  for (let n = 0; n < length; ++n) {\n    const n_reversed = length - n - 1;\n    result |= BigInt(input[n]) << 8n * BigInt(n_reversed);\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction getStringOption(options\x2C key) {\n  let value;\n  if (options && (value = options[key]) != null)\n    validateString(value\x2C `options.${key}`);\n  return value;\n}\n\n// Must be at most 31 entries.\nconst kCanonicalUsageOrder = [\n  'encrypt'\x2C 'decrypt'\x2C\n  'sign'\x2C 'verify'\x2C\n  'deriveKey'\x2C 'deriveBits'\x2C\n  'wrapKey'\x2C 'unwrapKey'\x2C\n  'encapsulateKey'\x2C 'encapsulateBits'\x2C\n  'decapsulateKey'\x2C 'decapsulateBits'\x2C\n];\n\nconst kUsageMasks = {\n  __proto__: null\x2C\n};\nconst kUsageByMask = {\n  __proto__: null\x2C\n};\n// Derive both lookup tables from kCanonicalUsageOrder so adding a new\n// usage only requires updating the canonical list above. The numeric\n// mask uses the usage's canonical index as its bit position.\nfor (let n = 0; n < kCanonicalUsageOrder.length; n++) {\n  const usage = kCanonicalUsageOrder[n];\n  const mask = 1 << n;\n  kUsageMasks[usage] = mask;\n  kUsageByMask[mask] = usage;\n}\n\n/**\n * Collects a key usage list into a set.\n * @param {string[]} usages\n * @returns {SafeSet<string>}\n */\nfunction toUsagesSet(usages) {\n  const usagesSet = new SafeSet();\n  for (let n = 0; n < usages.length; n++) {\n    usagesSet.add(usages[n]);\n  }\n  return usagesSet;\n}\n\n/**\n * Returns a bit mask representing the usages from `usageSet`.\n * @param {SafeSet<string>} usageSet\n * @returns {number}\n */\nfunction getUsagesMask(usageSet) {\n  // No usages is a valid state for some public keys\x2C represented by a\n  // zero mask.\n  if (usageSet.size === 0) return 0;\n  let mask = 0;\n  for (const usage of usageSet) {\n    mask |= kUsageMasks[usage];\n  }\n  return mask;\n}\n\n/**\n * Returns whether `mask` contains `usage`.\n * @param {number} mask\n * @param {string} usage\n * @returns {boolean}\n */\nfunction hasUsage(mask\x2C usage) {\n  return (mask & kUsageMasks[usage]) !== 0;\n}\n\n/**\n * Returns the usages represented by `mask` in canonical order.\n * @param {number} mask\n * @returns {string[]}\n */\nfunction getUsagesFromMask(mask) {\n  // Short circuit most common cases\x2C empty and single usage\n  // No usages is a valid state for some public keys\n  if (mask === 0) return [];\n  // A mask with exactly one bit set maps directly to one usage\n  if ((mask & (mask - 1)) === 0) {\n    return [kUsageByMask[mask]];\n  }\n  // Multiple usages need to be expanded in canonical order.\n  const result = [];\n  for (let n = 0; n < kCanonicalUsageOrder.length; n++) {\n    if (mask & (1 << n))\n      ArrayPrototypePush(result\x2C kCanonicalUsageOrder[n]);\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction getBlockSize(name) {\n  switch (name) {\n    case 'SHA-1':\n      // Fall through\n    case 'SHA-256':\n      return 512;\n    case 'SHA-384':\n      // Fall through\n    case 'SHA-512':\n      return 1024;\n    case 'SHA3-256':\n      // Fall through\n    case 'SHA3-384':\n      // Fall through\n    case 'SHA3-512':\n      // This interaction is not defined for now.\n      // https://github.com/WICG/webcrypto-modern-algos/issues/23\n      throw lazyDOMException('Explicit algorithm length member is required'\x2C 'NotSupportedError');\n  }\n}\n\nfunction getDigestSizeInBytes(name) {\n  switch (name) {\n    case 'SHA-1':\n      return 20;\n    case 'SHA-256': // Fall through\n    case 'SHA3-256':\n      return 32;\n    case 'SHA-384': // Fall through\n    case 'SHA3-384':\n      return 48;\n    case 'SHA-512': // Fall through\n    case 'SHA3-512':\n      return 64;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateKeyOps(keyOps\x2C usagesSet) {\n  if (keyOps === undefined) return;\n  validateArray(keyOps\x2C 'keyData.key_ops');\n  let keyOpsMask = 0;\n  for (let n = 0; n < keyOps.length; n++) {\n    const op = keyOps[n];\n    const opMask = kUsageMasks[op];\n    // Skipping unknown key ops\n    if (opMask === undefined)\n      continue;\n    // Have we seen it already? if so\x2C error\n    if (keyOpsMask & opMask)\n      throw lazyDOMException('Duplicate key operation'\x2C 'DataError');\n    keyOpsMask |= opMask;\n\n    // TODO(@jasnell): RFC7517 section 4.3 strong recommends validating\n    // key usage combinations. Specifically\x2C it says that unrelated key\n    // ops SHOULD NOT be used together. We're not yet validating that here.\n  }\n\n  if (usagesSet !== undefined) {\n    const usagesMask = getUsagesMask(usagesSet);\n    if ((keyOpsMask & usagesMask) !== usagesMask) {\n      throw lazyDOMException(\n        'Key operations and usage mismatch'\x2C\n        'DataError');\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction secureHeapUsed() {\n  const val = _secureHeapUsed();\n  if (val === undefined)\n    return { total: 0\x2C used: 0\x2C utilization: 0\x2C min: 0 };\n  const used = Number(_secureHeapUsed());\n  const total = Number(getOptionValue('--secure-heap'));\n  const min = Number(getOptionValue('--secure-heap-min'));\n  const utilization = used / total;\n  return { total\x2C used\x2C utilization\x2C min };\n}\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  getArrayBufferOrView\x2C\n  getBufferSourceByteLength\x2C\n  getBufferSourceBytes\x2C\n  getCiphers\x2C\n  getCurves\x2C\n  getDataViewOrTypedArrayBuffer\x2C\n  getHashes\x2C\n  getOptionalByteLength\x2C\n  kHandle\x2C\n  setEngine\x2C\n  toBuf\x2C\n\n  kNamedCurveAliases\x2C\n  kSupportedAlgorithms\x2C\n  normalizeAlgorithm\x2C\n  normalizeHashName\x2C\n  hasAnyNotIn\x2C\n  validateByteSource\x2C\n  validateKeyOps\x2C\n  jobPromise\x2C\n  jobPromiseThen\x2C\n  cleanupWebCryptoResult\x2C\n  prepareWebCryptoResult\x2C\n  validateMaxBufferLength\x2C\n  numBitsToBytes\x2C\n  truncateToBitLength\x2C\n  bigIntArrayToUnsignedBigInt\x2C\n  bigIntArrayToUnsignedInt\x2C\n  getBlockSize\x2C\n  getDigestSizeInBytes\x2C\n  getStringOption\x2C\n  getUsagesMask\x2C\n  getUsagesFromMask\x2C\n  toUsagesSet\x2C\n  hasUsage\x2C\n  secureHeapUsed\x2C\n  getCachedHashId\x2C\n  getHashCache\x2C\n  getOpenSSLSecLevel\x2C\n};\n
